Subject: [PATCH] 2810: the owner's own next line records a search as accepted
 or refused
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MASTER TEST RUN AD-015 (8 Oct, 2 of 2): „კი, ზუსტად ეს მჭირდებოდა, მადლობა."
after a search that named the right contact left the search with no
outcome; „successful searches" stayed 0 (0 of 7,588 on record). The model
never calls record_search_outcome.

At the start of a run, the owner's line is read against the newest search
of the conversation that returned people: a word about the result itself
(„ზუსტად", „ეს მჭირდებოდა", "exactly", "perfect"), or a yes together with
thanks, records „accepted"; „ეს არ არის…", "not what I needed" records
„refused". A bare „კი" records nothing — the reply to a search often ends
with another question (T2181). Only an unset outcome is written; a rung the
owner climbed is never overwritten. Read before the server's own thanks
answer can return. No new text.

